    return (...args) => {
        if (!hasBeenCalled) {
            hasBeenCalled = true;
            return fn(...args);
        }
        return null;
    };
}
```

This decorator function takes a function as its parameter and creates a closure that captures the state of whether the function has been executed before. On the first call to the decorated function, the `hasBeenCalled` variable is set to `true`, and the original function is invoked with the provided arguments. Subsequent calls to the decorated function simply return `null`.
